-- title:
--   Point With Complete Part As Switcheroo Input
-- statement:
--   **A point-with-complete-part relation is the switcheroo point-product relation.**
--
--   Suppose the complete-part point-product left and right families satisfy an `SDDOpRel` bound with error `gamma` over uniform slice-pair questions. Reinterpreting their outcome type as `Polynomial params x Unit`, and using the complete-part projection family, gives the exact switcheroo point-product relation:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDOpRel}\!\left(\psi_{bi},\mathcal D,
--   \mathrm{switcherooPointProductLeft},
--   \mathrm{switcherooPointProductRight},\gamma\right).
--   $$
--
--   No numerical error changes. The theorem only changes the presentation of the families and their outcome indexing so that the relation matches the input expected by `CommutativitySwitcherooStatement`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.pointWithCompletePart_as_switcheroo_input`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
